---
// Problem Section - General Observations (Strict Meta Compliance: No "Are you...?" statements)
---

<section class="section section-problem" aria-label="The Reality of Starting From Home">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="problem-card">
      <div class="problem-header">
        <span class="section-label">The Reality Today</span>
        <h2>Why Getting Started Usually Feels So Heavy</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-content">
        <p class="problem-lead">
          Starting something independent from home should feel encouraging. Yet for most people exploring new options, the reality online looks quite different:
        </p>

        <ul class="problem-points" role="list">
          <li class="problem-point">
            <div class="point-icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
                <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
                <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Endless conflicting noise:</strong> One person insists you need complicated sales funnels, another says you need daily video dances, and a third pushes expensive monthly subscriptions.
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="problem-point">
            <div class="point-icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
                <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Strictly limited quiet time:</strong> When free hours have to be carved out in small pockets around existing daily responsibilities, there is zero margin for complex technical setups that take weeks to figure out.
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="problem-point">
            <div class="point-icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Fatigue from unrealistic hype:</strong> The internet is flooded with overnight claims and questionable schemes, making it exhausting to identify what is actually grounded, honest, and legitimate.
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="problem-point">
            <div class="point-icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <polygon points="12 2 2 7 12 12 22 7 12 2"></polygon>
                <polyline points="2 17 12 22 22 17"></polyline>
                <polyline points="2 12 12 17 22 12"></polyline>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>Decision paralysis:</strong> Trying to evaluate endless different business ideas all at once usually results in researching for months without ever launching a single offer.
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="problem-takeaway">
          <p>
            The barrier is rarely ability or effort. The real problem is having too much scattered information and not enough quiet clarity.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section-problem {
    background-color: var(--bg-surface-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);
  }

  .problem-card {
    background: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-medium);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2.25rem 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .problem-card {
      padding: 3rem 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  .problem-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .problem-header h2 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .problem-lead {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-body);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .problem-points {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .problem-point {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--bg-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text-body);
  }

  .point-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    background: var(--sage-100);
    color: var(--sage-800);
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .problem-takeaway {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--sage-50);
    border: 1px dashed var(--sage-300);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .problem-takeaway p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--sage-800);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
